    "title": "3D data of specimen MNHN.F.A97320",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.14856200",
    "publication_date": "2025-02-12",
    "description": "<p>This repository contains the 3D data from the paper&nbsp;<em>Synchrotron X-ray tomography sheds light on the phylogenetic affinities of the enigmatic thylacocephalans with Pancrustacea.&nbsp;</em>This includes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Original tomographic datasets (MNHN_F_A97320.raw) of the specimen. Phase-contrast synchrotron X-ray microtomography was performed at the PSICH&Eacute; beamline of the SOLEIL synchrotron (Saint-Aubin, France). The specimen was scanned with a voxel size of 11.139 &micro;m. The info file (MNHN_F_A97320_b_0_pag.raw.info) contains the information concerning the dimension of the voxels.<br><br></li>\n<li>The segmentation files (mimics files). Segmentation was performed using Materialise Mimics innovation suite 24.0 (research edition).&nbsp; Segmentation was mostly achieved through manual segmentation of selected slices and interpolation between these slices. When possible, semi-automatic segmentation tools were used, in particular thresholding associated with region grow function to separate objects of similar attenuation.<br><br></li>\n<li>The triangle-mesh models of the specimen (STL files) resulting from the segmentation and the 3D rendering. Cleaning (<em>remove isolated pieces</em>, <em>remove duplicated faces</em> functions), reorientation (<em>re-orient all face coherently</em> function) and remeshing filters (<em>repair non Manifold edges</em>, <em>close holes </em>and <em>quadric edge collapse decimation </em>functions with preserve normal and topology checked) were applied.</li>\n</ul>",
